{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And he shall do for the bull</b> — this — <b>as he did for the bull of the sin-offering.</b> As is spelled out in the section of the anointed priest — to bring the caul and the two kidneys that were specified there, which are not specified here; and to repeat the rules of the service-offerings, to teach that if he omitted one of all the gifts it is invalid. For we find regarding the gifts on the outer altar that he offered them in a single application and achieved atonement; therefore it was necessary to state here that the omission of any one of them disqualifies (Leviticus 5:39)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:04:56.781909824Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}